TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Reproduced checkpoint cp-smoke locally and traced its exit 1 to two defects in the harness script scripts/run-smoke.sh, not to the engine under test: (1) the probe `podman run --rm --device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host -v .../results:/results \"$IMAGE\" python3 - <<'PY'` omits `-i`/`--interactive`, so podman never forwards the heredoc to the container's stdin; `python3 -` reads immediate EOF, executes nothing, prints nothing and exits 0, so `set -euo pipefail` does not trip, no receipt is written to results/receipts/ or results/receipts/failed/, and the trailing verifier heredoc exits 1 because results/receipts/smoke.json is absent. This exactly matches the captured evidence: stdout contains only the `smoke receipt: ...` echo line, stderr is empty, and the worktree has no results/receipts/smoke.json (only build.json, weights-coordinator.json, weights-worker.json). Confirmed by direct A/B: `podman run --rm flashnext:dev python3 - <<<'print(...)'` prints nothing and exits 0, while the same command with `-i` prints. (2) After forwarding stdin with an identical payload against a scratch /results mount, four of five probes pass on this host (arch gcn_arch=gfx1151, on_cdna=false, supports_fp8_stock_predicate=false; fp8_cast e4m3fn_alloc_and_cast=true; registry model_arch_registered=true; aperture ttm_pages_limit=33554432) but `admission()` raises `TypeError: cannot unpack non-iterable bool object`, setting the receipt status to fail. The engine-side patch is correct and is not the fault: the run logs `TritonExperts: admitting block-FP8 fused MoE (...) on gfx1151 via in-kernel bf16 upcast`, and `inspect.signature(TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme)` is `(weight_key: QuantKey | None, activation_key: QuantKey | None) -> bool`. The smoke probe wrongly destructures that bool as a two-tuple `ok, why`. Both defects are in the checkpoint script itself; cp-smoke is a checkpoint task whose brief forbids modifying the repository and whose kind never retries, so the fix must land as a separate amendment task owning scripts/run-smoke.sh. The repository was left unmodified (git status clean at 1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304).","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/run-smoke.sh"],"goal":"Repair the two harness defects in scripts/run-smoke.sh so the in-container smoke actually executes its probes and reports a truthful receipt. First, add -i (or --interactive) to the `podman run` invocation so the quoted heredoc payload reaches `python3 -` inside the container; without it the container is a silent no-op that exits 0 and writes no receipt. Second, fix the `admission()` probe: `TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme(weight_key, activation_key)` returns a plain bool, not an (ok, why) pair, so replace the two-target unpack with a single bool capture and derive the human-readable reason separately (for example from the hasattr fallback string, or by reporting the admitted/refused state directly). Keep the existing hasattr guard semantics so a build lacking the hook still reports fp8_block_moe_admitted=false with a reason rather than crashing. Do not weaken any probe into an unconditional pass, do not delete probes, and do not change the D12 receipt-quarantine behaviour (pass receipts to results/receipts/smoke.json, fail receipts to results/receipts/failed/smoke.json, exit code unchanged) or the trailing verifier heredoc's contract. Do not modify the vLLM fork, the container overlay, or any patches under patches/ — the engine already admits the block-FP8 fused MoE scheme on gfx1151 and is not at fault.","acceptance":[{"id":"podman-stdin-forwarded","description":"The podman run invocation in scripts/run-smoke.sh passes -i or --interactive so the heredoc payload is forwarded to the container's stdin.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -qE '(^|[[:space:]])(-i|--interactive)([[:space:]]|$)' <(sed -n '/^podman run/,/^ *\"\\$IMAGE\"/p' scripts/run-smoke.sh)"]},{"id":"admission-no-tuple-unpack","description":"The admission() probe no longer destructures the bool return of _supports_quant_scheme into a two-element tuple.","argv":["bash","-c","! grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*ok,[[:space:]]*why[[:space:]]*=' scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},{"id":"smoke-runs-and-passes","description":"scripts/run-smoke.sh executes end to end against the built flashnext:dev image and exits 0.","argv":["bash","scripts/run-smoke.sh"]},{"id":"smoke-receipt-status-pass","description":"After the run, results/receipts/smoke.json exists with status pass, no quarantined fail receipt remains, and every probe key is present with fp8_block_moe_admitted true, e4m3fn_alloc_and_cast true, and model_arch_registered true.","argv":["python3","-c","import json,os,sys;assert not os.path.exists('results/receipts/failed/smoke.json'),'stale fail receipt present';r=json.load(open('results/receipts/smoke.json'));d=r['data'];assert r['status']=='pass',r;assert set(('arch','fp8_cast','registry','aperture','admission'))<=set(d),d;assert all(not isinstance(v,str) or not v.startswith('FAIL:') for v in d.values()),d;assert d['fp8_cast']['e4m3fn_alloc_and_cast'] is True,d;assert d['registry']['model_arch_registered'] is True,d;assert d['admission']['fp8_block_moe_admitted'] is True,d;print('ok')"]},{"id":"quarantine-contract-intact","description":"The D12 receipt-quarantine branch and the trailing verifier heredoc are still present in the script.","argv":["bash","-c","grep -q 'results/receipts/failed' scripts/run-smoke.sh && grep -q '/results/receipts. if r..status.. == .pass.' scripts/run-smoke.sh"]}],"dependencies":["cp-build"]}}
